Subject: [PATCH] topaz: never allocate from the unmanaged GPU pool in midmem mode

The fixed GPU pool 0x90000000..0xd0000000 overlaps the 3 GiB ADT's
XNU-managed bank 0x82000000..0x140000000. With gpu_midmem=1 all GPU
buffers must use the existing IOKit allocation paths; an allocation failure
must not fall back to this fixed pool. Use gpu_fbpool=0 for display buffers.

--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazAdreno.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/TopazAdreno.cpp
@@ -245,6 +245,12 @@
 {
 	uint64_t pa;
 
+	/* --midmem gives this bank to XNU. A fixed physical pool would alias live
+	 * kernel pages; callers must use their IOKit allocation path or fail. */
+	if (gpu_midmem != 0) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	size = (size + GPU_POOL_UNIT - 1) & ~(GPU_POOL_UNIT - 1);
 	if (size > GPU_POOL_CHUNK - GPU_POOL_UNIT) {
 		return 0;
